      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>That's a pretty strong stance. You're saying that the focus on social justice effectively turns art into propaganda? I'm curious where the line is drawn—is there any way for art to be politically engaged without losing its aesthetic value, or do you think those two goals are fundamentally at odds?",
